  "id": "Compound::DB08871 - Gene::203068",
  "verbalization": "Eribulin's relationship with Tubb is supported by a series of molecular interactions that converge through the shared pathway of microtubule inhibition. The evidence suggests that Eribulin, through its inclusion in the microtubule inhibition class, binds to Tubb8, which in turn binds to Tubb. This indicates a potential mechanism where Eribulin may interact with Tubb via Tubb8, possibly through a common binding site or a shared structural feature. The lowest common ancestor of Eribulin and Vinorelbine, which is a Vinca-domain binding agent, further suggests a broader class of compounds that may interact with Tubb, reinforcing the idea that Eribulin's interaction with Tubb is part of a larger network of microtubule-targeting drugs. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Tubb as a downstream target in the microtubule inhibition cascade, with Eribulin potentially acting through a shared mechanism involving Tubb8 and Tubb.",
